# Export to Clipboard, row and tab menus, exact bytes. "Attached" means the
# thread's session is held by a PANE (the reference's live session): here t9
# is attached in the RIGHT pane while t2 holds the focused left pane. Export
# from t9's ROW writes t9's whole conversation -- "# <title>\n\n" then every
# loaded row as Copy Turn renders it, with no trailing trim -- not t2's, not
# the focused pane's -- and moves neither a thread nor keyboard focus: the
# caret is put in the focused pane's composer first (`composer_reply_input`
# names the FOCUSED pane's field; `expect_panes … 0` is the independent
# truth of WHICH pane that is) and shown to hold through idle frames, and
# both are asserted after each export. The same from
# t9's TAB menu. t6 offers the row DISABLED (dimmed) and a press writes
# nothing -- both as a kept BACKGROUND tab with cached history (the
# attachment boundary hanabi has and the reference does not: puffin_gaps.md
# Tabs & Windows #7; its preconditions are proven, not assumed) and as a
# never-opened row; Copy Deeplink beside it still works, so "disabled" is the
# gate and not the clipboard door. Rows are anchored by id: a thread's title
# is also its tab label while a tab is open.
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":["t2","t9"],"active_tab":"t2","split_open":true,"split_ratio":0.5,"split_panes":["t2","t9"],"split_focused_pane":0,"theme":"dark"}
# env: HANABI_OPEN=t2 HANABI_SPLIT=t9
require_thread t2
require_thread t9
expect_panes t2 t9 0
# Real keyboard focus: the focused pane's composer (pane 0 by expect_panes),
# stable before anything is exported.
click_ui composer_reply_input
wait_frames 6
expect_focused composer_reply_input
expect_panes t2 t9 0
wait_frames 30
expect_focused composer_reply_input
expect_panes t2 t9 0
reset_clipboard_probe

right_click_ui chat_row_id_t9
wait_frames 8
expect_text "Export to Clipboard"
expect_a11y "Export to Clipboard" says="Export to Clipboard, menuitem"
click_ui row_menu_export_clipboard
wait_frames 8
expect_clipboard_escaped "# kicker-tick\n\n*(recurring: kick the pending queue every ten minutes.)*\n\n### **Agentcloud**\n\nKicked 41 pending items. Draining what came back; nothing for you yet.\n\n"
expect_panes t2 t9 0
expect_focused composer_reply_input

reset_clipboard_probe
right_click_ui tab_t9
wait_frames 8
click_ui tab_menu_export_clipboard
wait_frames 8
expect_clipboard_escaped "# kicker-tick\n\n*(recurring: kick the pending queue every ten minutes.)*\n\n### **Agentcloud**\n\nKicked 41 pending items. Draining what came back; nothing for you yet.\n\n"
expect_panes t2 t9 0
expect_focused composer_reply_input

# The boundary the reference does not have (puffin_gaps.md Tabs & Windows
# #7): a thread OPEN in a kept background tab -- t6, whose transcript sits in
# the cache from its own load -- holds no live pane session in hanabi, so its
# row is DISABLED and a press writes nothing; no cache is read, nothing is
# fetched. Preconditions in order, each a receipt gated by a within= barrier
# (no fixed wait does the work): t6 opens as a PREVIEW, a second row click
# KEEPS it, the cache holds t6 with its two messages (an empty entry would
# not pass: min=2), its reply is DRAWN (a within= render receipt -- the cache
# filling is not the transcript rendering), then the pane is back on t2 with
# t6 still kept.
click_ui chat_row_id_t6
expect_open t6
expect_tab t6 preview within=60
# The second click on the same row KEEPS it (open_session_in_tab on an
# already-open thread: keep_tab + switch) -- the transition itself asserted,
# not just the end state. Every gating receipt is a within= consumer, so no
# later line dispatches ahead of it; the vendor's expect_text is not one and
# gates nothing here -- it follows the barrier that settled the attach.
click_ui chat_row_id_t6
expect_tab t6 kept within=60
expect_cached t6 min=2 within=60
# Cache readiness is not render readiness: the reply must be DRAWN before the
# pane moves on -- a within= receipt, so the tab switch cannot run ahead of
# the render it waits for (the vendor's expect_text is not a barrier). The
# phrase is one the transcript draws in a single run (the same fragment
# sidebar_opens_thread_in_tab asserts); the sentence as a whole is drawn in
# pieces and never registers as one text.
expect_text_drawn "61% through 2.1M rows" within=120
click_ui tab_t2
expect_panes t2 t9 0
expect_tab t6 kept within=60
reset_clipboard_probe
right_click_ui chat_row_id_t6
wait_frames 8
expect_a11y "Export to Clipboard" says="Export to Clipboard, menuitem, dimmed"
click_ui row_menu_export_clipboard
wait_frames 8
expect_clipboard ""
expect_text "CONVERSATION"
key ESCAPE
wait_frames 6

# Not attached to any pane and never opened: present, dimmed, inert.
reset_clipboard_probe
right_click_ui chat_row_id_t6
wait_frames 8
expect_text "Export to Clipboard"
expect_a11y "Export to Clipboard" says="Export to Clipboard, menuitem, dimmed"
click_ui row_menu_export_clipboard
wait_frames 8
expect_clipboard ""
expect_text "CONVERSATION"
click_ui row_menu_copy_deeplink
wait_frames 8
expect_clipboard "hanabi://thread/t6"
